{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure", "label": "ecs-rds-postgres-pool Infrastructure Plan (Plan 2)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Status complete 2026-09-22 with Tasks 2-16 executed; Task 1 Steps 3-4 (platform/ apply) and Task 17 (plan of infra/main) were deliberately deferred to plan 3 by the user's review decision, so nothing of the project exists yet in HCP or AWS."}, {"id": "infra_platform_workspace", "label": "platform/tfc.tf \u2014 TFC workspace registration", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "working_directory=infra/main is not cosmetic \u2014 it sets the upload root to the project directory, which is what makes ../grafana, ../k6 and ../../heartbeat resolve inside a remote HCP run. Amended in review to also carry db_password into the shared HCP variable set (ruling R19)."}, {"id": "infra_root_scaffolding", "label": "variables.tf / versions.tf \u2014 root module scaffolding", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deletes DynamoDB/pbkdf2/autoscaling/shedding/grafana_prom_* variables with no analogue and adds instance_class, pool_size, proxy_enabled, seed_rows, report_scan_rows, migrate_on_boot, seed_on_boot."}, {"id": "infra_generateslo_postgres_outputs", "label": "generate-slo.js Postgres outputs (renderQueries/renderClassMap)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two of five generated outputs (classmap.json, queries.json) don't depend on calibrated thresholds and are unblocked via a new --only-unblocked flag; sli_ratio only appears in queries.json once every class threshold is set. Amended during execution: native/exponential histograms have no _bucket suffix, so quantile queries use the bare metric name (ruling R5)."}, {"id": "infra_network_security_groups", "label": "network.tf \u2014 VPC, subnets, security groups incl. db", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Drops the DynamoDB gateway VPC endpoint entirely (RDS has no analogue) and adds a database security group; publicly_accessible plus a narrow group is a deliberate trade against paying for a NAT gateway. The db-group ingress rule changed twice during execution/review (R12 then superseded by R19, ending at 5432 open to 0.0.0.0/0)."}, {"id": "infra_rds_instance", "label": "rds.tf \u2014 aws_db_instance.main and teardown guards", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "skip_final_snapshot, backup_retention_period=0, delete_automated_backups, an explicitly-owned CloudWatch log group and parameter group are every C10 survivor guard made concrete; Performance Insights IS available on db.t4g.micro for PostgreSQL despite a widely repeated MySQL/MariaDB-only misconception, with db.t4g.medium as the named fallback."}, {"id": "infra_proxy_host_switch", "label": "proxy.tf \u2014 count-gated RDS Proxy and local.database_url switch", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every resource is count=var.proxy_enabled?1:0 so knob 3 is a one-line dev.tfvars edit and apply with no code/image/redeploy change; local.db_host switches between the instance address and the proxy endpoint. A pre-registered null-result expectation is written into the file before any run happens. Amended during execution to add an explicitly-owned, tagged proxy CloudWatch log group (ruling R13), matching the C10 survivor pattern RDS itself needed."}, {"id": "infra_ecr_alb", "label": "ecr.tf / alb.tf", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Copied verbatim from the sibling; the ALB's idle_timeout=60 must stay below the service's keepAliveTimeout/headersTimeout or the ALB can dispatch onto a connection Node is closing, producing a 502 that burns availability budget the service never spent."}, {"id": "infra_ecs_collector", "label": "ecs.tf + collector.tf + alloy.alloy.tftpl \u2014 service and OTLP collector", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Strips Alloy pipeline 2 (prometheus.exporter.cloudwatch for DynamoDB's SuccessfulRequestLatency) and its IAM/SSM plumbing since Postgres publishes no per-operation server-side latency to subtract; deletes the DynamoDB IAM statement entirely since Postgres auths via password in DATABASE_URL, not IAM. desired_count's lifecycle ignore_changes must be removed so every run is one deterministic Terraform-owned configuration, not autoscaler-adjusted."}, {"id": "infra_d1_canary_fork", "label": "Design decision D1: canary.tf is forked after all", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The spec's reason for dropping canary.tf ('a synthetic check, orthogonal to this project's question') doesn't match the file: its live resource is an sli_absent alert firing when the SLI series itself goes silent \u2014 an empty panel and a healthy system look identical otherwise, which is exactly the failure this repo's whole measurement discipline is built to avoid."}, {"id": "infra_d2_threshold_dependent_files", "label": "Design decision D2: threshold-dependent files can't exist yet", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slo.yaml ships with every threshold_ms null and validateSlo throws on that by design (plan 1); locals.tf/alerts.tf/slo.tf/k6 slo.js bake thresholds into PromQL/assertions and move entirely to plan 3, while classmap.json and queries.json (threshold-free) generate now via --only-unblocked."}, {"id": "infra_d3_cloudwatch_pipeline_removal", "label": "Design decision D3: dropping the CloudWatch pipeline removes more than the spec states", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Beyond the exporter block itself, the collector's CloudWatch-read IAM policy, the remote-write/scrape Alloy blocks, the three grafana_prom_* SSM-backed variables, and queries.json's cloudwatch_srl_by_operation/queueing_ms_by_route panels all become dead configuration if left in."}, {"id": "infra_d4_rds_ca_bundle", "label": "Design decision D4: image must trust both the RDS CA and public roots", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Knob 3 changes which certificate the service sees: the RDS CA (not in Node's default trust store) for a direct instance connection, vs. an ACM cert chaining to public roots for the proxy. Passing `ca` to TLS replaces rather than adds to the default store, so the fix is to trust [...tls.rootCertificates, rdsBundle] with rejectUnauthorized:true, keeping knob 3 a one-line tfvars change."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure", "label": "Infra plan (2026-09-21, plan 2)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md"}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_task9", "label": "Infra plan Task 9: The heartbeat", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md"}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_task10", "label": "Infra plan Task 10: Grafana module and dashboard", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md"}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_task11", "label": "Infra plan Task 11: Saturation rules", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md"}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_task12", "label": "Infra plan Task 12: The SLI-absent rule", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md"}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_task13", "label": "Infra plan Task 13: k6 module and load profiles", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md"}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_task14", "label": "Infra plan Task 14: The deploy script", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md"}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_task15", "label": "Infra plan Task 15: Verify the database certificate", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md"}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_task16", "label": "Infra plan Task 16: README, outputs, tfvars, spec amendment", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md"}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_task17", "label": "Infra plan Task 17: The reviewed plan", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md"}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_r8", "label": "Ruling R8: credit rule watches CPUSurplusCreditBalance", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "rationale": "CPUSurplusCreditsCharged only becomes non-zero after 24h of earning surplus or at termination, so on an instance destroyed daily it stays 0 through the event it is meant to catch; the surplus balance rises the moment surplus is spent."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_r9", "label": "Ruling R9: credit rule uses 300s/600s window", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "rationale": "T-class credit metrics publish every 5 minutes, so a 300s window is usually empty and no_data_state=OK would make the rule silent."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_r12", "label": "Ruling R12: DB security group admits self on 5432", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "rationale": "RDS Proxy ENIs sit in the same security group, so self-ingress lets the proxy reach the instance; superseded 2026-09-22 by R19's 0.0.0.0/0 rule."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_r14", "label": "Ruling R14: app_environment and database_target outputs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "rationale": "container_definitions prints as (sensitive value) in a plan because DATABASE_URL interpolates the generated password, so two non-sensitive outputs answer the review questions instead."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_r16", "label": "Ruling R16: operator_cidr as gitignored auto.tfvars (reversed)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "rationale": "dev.tfvars is committed in a public repo, so a personal IP must live in a gitignored *.auto.tfvars file; reversed 2026-09-22 by R19 which opens the DB to any address instead."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_r17", "label": "Ruling R17: pool_connection_timeout_ms has no default", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "rationale": "A 900ms default described as 'just above the heavy threshold' invented a threshold while every class threshold was null; with no default it cannot be forgotten."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_r19", "label": "Ruling R19: DB open to 0.0.0.0/0, guarded by password", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "rationale": "User chose psql access from any network with nothing personal to maintain over R16's operator_cidr approach, accepted for a lab of generated rows destroyed after each session."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_r20", "label": "Ruling R20: posts table not reset, size recorded", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "rationale": "20% of the mix inserts and the heartbeat inserts every minute so the table grows; recording SELECT count(*) FROM posts before each run is cheaper than building a reset that is not idempotent-safe."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure_d1_canary", "label": "Infra plan decision D1: canary.tf is forked, not synthetic", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "rationale": "canary.tf's live resource alerts when the SLI series goes absent, guarding against a silent pipeline -- the failure this project can least afford."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure", "label": "Plan: ecs-rds-postgres-pool infrastructure (2026-09-21)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_09_19_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_design", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_21_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_infrastructure", "target": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_20_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_service", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "infra_proxy_host_switch", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_d5_second_knob", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.9}, {"source": "infra_proxy_host_switch", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_c4_rds_proxy_effect", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.9}, {"source": "infra_proxy_host_switch", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_c5_max_connections_cliff", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.85}, {"source": "infra_rds_instance", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_c6_cpu_credits", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.85}, {"source": "infra_rds_instance", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_c10_teardown_survivors", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.9}, {"source": "infra_network_security_groups", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_c8_reaching_database", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.9}, {"source": "infra_d4_rds_ca_bundle", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_c9_tls_credentials", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.85}, {"source": "infra_root_scaffolding", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_d2_instance_class", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.85}, {"source": "infra_root_scaffolding", "target": "docs_research_ecs_rds_postgres_pool_d4_migrations_seed", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.8, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.8}, {"source": "infra_root_scaffolding", "target": "infra_platform_workspace", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastructure.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.9}, {"source": "infra_generateslo_postgres_outputs", "target": "service_generateslo_validateslo", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-21-ecs-rds-postgres-pool-infrastruc